ion (v), and the Rule-5 command-output exemption (x)), and the plan does not require the entry to state the disambiguator — namely that re-running the gate is the antipattern only when a DIFFERENT unit is under test and the gate is invoked as a proxy, whereas asserting a gate script's own exit code/output when the gate script IS the unit under test is a legitimate behaviour test.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f494b061c5b0ee64f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC3 (gate-script re-run entry)","norm_id":"nb0e79cd97b7fe2a3","priority":0.5025,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test that runs scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py (the gate IS the unit under test) and asserts its exit code / output — legitimate per guard (iii)/(v) — gets flagged by the new gate-script re-run entry because the entry lacks a disambiguator","A reviewer cannot tell whether the gate script is the unit under test or merely a proxy, so the new entry and guards (iii)/(v)/(x) give contradictory verdicts on the same diff"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to AC3 that the entry must state: 'Litmus: is the gate script itself the unit under test (then its exit-code/output assertion is valid per guards iii/v), or is some other unit under test and the whole gate re-run as a proxy for it (then it is this antipattern)?' and that a corresponding FP-gatererun-* case covers a legitimate exit-code assertion on the gate-as-unit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_